<title>RUSSIA: Russian 1997 spring sowing stays ahead of 1996.</title>
<headline>Russian 1997 spring sowing stays ahead of 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's 1997 spring sowing campaign continues to outpace 1996 levels, with 1.43 million hectares sown by April 14, 46 percent higher than at the same time last year, the State Statistics Committee said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Grains accounted for 941,000 hectares of the total area sown, 74 percent higher than year-ago levels. This did not include the area sown to maize, the committee said.</p>
<p>Sugar beet sowings had reached 121,000 hectares by April 14, seven percent ahead of the same period last year.</p>
